@startuml HRMS_RLS_Model
title HRMS PostgreSQL - Tenant RLS Model

actor "User / Worker" as User
participant "Node.js API / FastAPI Worker" as App
database "PostgreSQL Connection" as Conn
database "PostgreSQL RLS" as RLS
database "Tenant Table" as Data

User -> App: Request / Event
App -> Conn: BEGIN
App -> Conn: SET LOCAL app.tenant_id = tenant-A
Conn -> RLS: SELECT employee WHERE ...
RLS -> RLS: Evaluate tenant policy
RLS -> Data: tenant_id = app.tenant_id
Data --> RLS: Matching rows only
RLS --> Conn: Tenant-scoped result
Conn --> App: Result
App -> Conn: COMMIT

note over App,RLS
The tenant context must be transaction-local.
Do not keep tenant_id as a persistent connection setting.
Connection pools may reuse connections across tenants.
end note

note over User,App
SQS worker messages must carry tenant_id because
there is no HTTP JWT in a background worker.
end note

@enduml
